WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.616
Some content belongs on a map, such as a shop, an office, or a venue.

00:00:05.616 --> 00:00:09.616
The Geo Point field stores that location on a content item.

00:00:09.616 --> 00:00:14.970
In this video, you enable the Spatial feature, add the field, and set a location.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:22.497
A shop, an office, or a venue has a place.

00:00:22.497 --> 00:00:26.826
A Geo Point field keeps that place on the content item itself, as

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:30.180
numbers that an editor can type or pick on a map.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.207
The field stores two numbers:

00:00:33.207 --> 00:00:35.354
a latitude and a longitude.

00:00:35.354 --> 00:00:40.169
The Latitude box takes values from minus 90 to 90, and the Longitude

00:00:40.169 --> 00:00:42.251
box from minus 180 to 180.

00:00:42.251 --> 00:00:45.830
Both can stay empty unless the field is required.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.790
The editor comes in two forms.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:53.334
Standard shows the two boxes, and Leaflet editor adds a map, where a

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:55.237
click fills in the boxes.

00:00:55.237 --> 00:01:00.640
The map background comes from OpenStreetMap, so the browser needs internet access.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.108
Let's open Tools, Features, and search for Spatial.

00:01:08.108 --> 00:01:11.308
Its row lists the features it depends on directly:

00:01:11.308 --> 00:01:13.080
Content Types and Lucene.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.913
Let's select Enable.

00:01:14.913 --> 00:01:18.185
A message confirms that the feature Spatial was enabled.

00:01:18.185 --> 00:01:21.510
Lucene is enabled with it, because Spatial depends on it.

00:01:25.744 --> 00:01:29.250
Let's open Design, Content Definition, Content Types.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:33.884
We add the field to the Page content type, so we select Edit on its row.

00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:36.794
Under Fields, we select Add Field.

00:01:36.794 --> 00:01:41.876
We type Location as the Display Name, and the Technical Name follows from it.

00:01:41.876 --> 00:01:45.244
Then we choose Geo Point Field as the Field Type.

00:01:45.724 --> 00:01:47.683
We select Save & Configure.

00:01:47.683 --> 00:01:53.622
The field's settings include Required, which makes both coordinates mandatory, and Hint, which

00:01:53.622 --> 00:01:57.244
shows help text under the Latitude and Longitude boxes.

00:01:57.702 --> 00:02:02.180
Each box is labeled only Latitude or Longitude, so a hint tells editors

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:04.332
which location the field holds.

00:02:04.332 --> 00:02:06.892
Let's check Required and write a hint.

00:02:07.349 --> 00:02:12.594
Further down the settings page, the editor list offers Standard, with two number

00:02:12.594 --> 00:02:15.643
boxes, and Leaflet editor, which adds a map.

00:02:15.643 --> 00:02:18.509
We choose Leaflet editor and select Save.

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:23.165
Back on the Page content type, the Location field is listed as a

00:02:23.165 --> 00:02:26.701
Geo Point Field, with a Leaflet badge for its editor.

00:02:30.951 --> 00:02:35.410
Let's open Content, Content Items, select New, and choose Page.

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:37.671
We type Find Us as the title.

00:02:39.838 --> 00:02:42.420
We scroll down below the page content.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:46.528
The field shows a Latitude box, a Longitude box, and a map, with

00:02:46.528 --> 00:02:48.288
the hint under each box.

00:02:48.831 --> 00:02:51.139
Clicking the map chooses a place.

00:02:51.139 --> 00:02:55.164
The boxes fill in with six decimal places, and a marker with a

00:02:55.164 --> 00:02:56.821
popup shows the point.

00:02:57.355 --> 00:03:01.838
To be exact, we type the values ourselves, and the marker follows what we type.

00:03:01.838 --> 00:03:04.265
Let's enter the coordinates of our shop.

00:03:04.764 --> 00:03:06.072
We select Publish.

00:03:06.072 --> 00:03:10.544
A message confirms that your Page has been published, and the list shows it.

00:03:14.844 --> 00:03:17.208
We select Edit on the Find Us row.

00:03:17.208 --> 00:03:22.884
Because the field has values, the map opens centered on the saved location, with a marker.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.803
Back in the list, we select View.

00:03:25.803 --> 00:03:28.445
The site shows the location as text:

00:03:28.445 --> 00:03:33.290
the latitude, a comma, and the longitude, each with six decimal places.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:42.140
The location is stored with the content item and shown on the site as text.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:46.561
When the content type belongs to a Lucene index and the field's setting

00:03:46.561 --> 00:03:52.130
Include this element in the index is checked, developers can search by area or by distance.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:58.309
The Geo Point field keeps a location with a content item, entered as

00:03:58.309 --> 00:04:00.511
two numbers or by clicking a map.

00:04:00.511 --> 00:04:01.980
Thanks for watching.

